esources and Fire & Rescue Overview and Scrutiny Committee","date":"01/07/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-28","committee":"Warwickshire Fire and Rescue Local Pension Board of the Firefighters' Pension Scheme","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-29","committee":"Children & Young People Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-30","committee":"Resources and Fire & Rescue Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-15","committee":"Cabinet","time":"1.45 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Warwickshire Local Pension Board","time":"11.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-02","committee":"Warwickshire Fire and Rescue Local Pension Board of the Firefighters' Pension Scheme","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-04","committee":"Children & Young People Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-12","committee":"Cabinet","time":"1.45 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Audit and Standards Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-22","committee":"Children & Young People Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Communities Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Adult Social Care and Health Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"County Council","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":true,"url":"https://democracy.warwickshire.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Pension fund prepares first-ever comprehensive budget and medium-term financial plan","lead":"The lack of a systematic budget and MTFP prior to 2026/27 suggests prior gaps in financial oversight. As this is the first iteration, forecast accuracy is unproven.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Business Plan Monitoring Quarter 1","paper_url":"https://warwickshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50908/50908.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Pension fund governance compliance rated amber due to volume of work required in a short timeframe","lead":"Governance weaknesses in pension fund management could create compliance risk and signal capacity constraints across the council's operations.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Business Plan Monitoring Quarter 1","paper_url":"https://warwickshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50908/50908.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Pension fund expected to run cashflow negative over 2026/27\u20132029/30 with benefit payments exceeding contributions","lead":"A lender must understand whether the council has sufficient reserves to sustain pension fund operations and whether reserve drawdowns are affecting its financial resilience.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Business Plan Monitoring Quarter 1","paper_url":"https://warwickshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50908/50908.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"LGPS Pension Fund Sub-Committee","paper_title":"Business Plan Monitoring Quarter 1","paper_url":"https://warwickshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50908/50908.pdf","headline":"Pension fund prepares first-ever comprehensive budget and medium-term financial plan","detail":"A fund-wide budget and three-year MTFP has been prepared for the first time. Quarter 1 actual results have been reviewed against budget assumptions to validate forecasts. The paper notes the absence of prior established budget monitoring history at this level.","category":"governance","matters":"The lack of a systematic budget and MTFP prior to 2026/27 suggests prior gaps in financial oversight. As this is the first iteration, forecast accuracy is unproven.","figures":"None","quote":"A budget and 3 year Medium-Term Financial Plan (MTFP) has been prepared for the Fund for the first time. Given the absence of an established budget monitoring history at this level, the initial budget assumptions against Quarter 1 have been reviewed against actual expenditure and cash flow activity","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"LGPS Pension Fund Sub-Committee","paper_title":"Business Plan Monitoring Quarter 1","paper_url":"https://warwickshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50908/50908.pdf","headline":"Pension fund governance compliance rated amber due to volume of work required in a short timeframe","detail":"The fund faces multiple overlapping governance demands from the AON governance review, Pension Schemes Act 2026, Local Government Reorganisation, and administration projects including the pensions dashboard and access/fairness initiatives, creating significant delivery risk.","category":"governance","matters":"Governance weaknesses in pension fund management could create compliance risk and signal capacity constraints across the council's operations.","figures":"None","quote":"the overall volume of governance development activity that is required in a short space of time (the actions from the AON governance review, actions from the Pension Schemes Act 2026, Local Government Reorganisation, and the various projects required of the administration service)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"LGPS Pension Fund Sub-Committee","paper_title":"Business Plan Monitoring Quarter 1","paper_url":"https://warwickshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50908/50908.pdf","headline":"Pension fund expected to run cashflow negative over 2026/27\u20132029/30 with benefit payments exceeding contributions","detail":"Benefit payments and associated expenditure will exceed contribution income each year, requiring funding from cash reserves and/or partial investment redemption. The paper notes this reflects natural fund maturity but requires robust cash management and sufficient liquidity.","category":"reserves","matters":"A lender must understand whether the council has sufficient reserves to sustain pension fund operations and whether reserve drawdowns are affecting its financial resilience.","figures":"cashflow negative across planning period","quote":"the Fund is expected overall to be cash flow negative over the planning period, with benefit payments and associated expenditure exceeding contribution income. The forecast shortfall will be funded from existing cash reserves and/or the partial redemption of investments","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"LGPS Pension Fund Sub-Committee","paper_title":"Business Plan Monitoring Quarter 1","paper_url":"https://warwickshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50908/50908.pdf","headline":"Pension fund to add \u00a3272k in annual staffing costs","detail":"The fund requires three new pension officers and one assistant (\u00a3169k) for business-as-usual demand, a governance officer (\u00a345k) for compliance reforms, and a project manager (\u00a358k) for coordination of governance reforms, LGR, and administration projects. These are flagged as new costs over existing commitments.","category":"other","matters":"New recurring staffing costs either drain the pension fund reserves or require increased employer contributions from the council, affecting its general fund budget.","figures":"\u00a3169k, \u00a345k, \u00a358k","quote":"Administration Team 3 Pension Officers and 1 Pension Assistant to meet underlying business as usual demand levels: \u00a3169k. Governance Officer post to support growth in governance demands (General Code of Practice, Fit for the Future reforms): \u00a345k.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"LGPS Pension Fund Sub-Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 3 for Pension Fund Governance Report","paper_url":"https://warwickshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50902/50902.pdf","headline":"The Fund has statutory powers to recover administration costs from employers failing to meet their pension obligations, with specific financial penalties.","detail":"Under LGPS Regulation 70, the Fund can charge employers for poor performance including late contributions (\u00a3500 per occurrence plus 1% above base rate interest), late data submissions (\u00a31,000 plus \u00a3100 per week), and persistent data quality problems (\u00a350 per case). The Fund also recharges any Pensions Regulator or Pensions Ombudsman fines in full to the responsible employer. Improvement notices must be issued before enforcement.","category":"governance","matters":"These cost recovery powers indicate the Fund has formal enforcement mechanisms for employer compliance. For councils with governance weaknesses or cash flow problems, such charges could represent material unforeseen costs.","figures":"\u00a3500 per late contribution plus interest; \u00a31,000 plus \u00a3100/week for late year-end returns; \u00a350 plus \u00a350/month for late starter information.","quote":"Where a serious or persistent and on-going failure to deliver employer responsibilities to the Fund occurs (for example late contributions, late data submissions, or poor data quality), and no improvement is demonstrated by an Employer the Fund may recover costs from an Employer.","material":false}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-14"},"name":"Warwickshire CC","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-25","since_iso":"2026-08-26","distress":false,"headline":"Pension fund prepares first-ever comprehensive budget and medium-term financial plan","lead":"The lack of a systematic budget and MTFP prior to 2026/27 suggests prior gaps in financial oversight. As this is the first iteration, forecast accuracy is unproven.","also":["55 other findings in this window","14 papers caught"],"watch":"Children & Young People Overview and Scrutiny Committee on 2026-09-29","n_findings":56,"n_documents":14,"top_paper_title":"Business Plan Monitoring Quarter 1","top_paper_url":"https://warwickshire.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s50908/50908.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":119,"news_drafts_total":3}}